---
title: Incline Dumbbell Flyes (30°)
type: docs
prev: docs/grud/
---
![разведение гантелей на наклонной (30) вверх скамье](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3e2438f2-8b32-4549-a8fa-a109088f1ca1)

{{% steps %}}

### Step 1
Grab a pair of dumbbells and lie back on a bench set to a 30-degree incline.

### Step 2
Raise the dumbbells above your chest, keeping a slight, fixed bend in your elbows.

### Step 3
Turn your hands so your palms face inward toward each other. This is your starting position.

### Step 4
Inhale and slowly open your arms out to the sides in a wide arc until your elbows are roughly level with your shoulders.

### Step 5
Exhale, squeeze your chest muscles, and bring the dumbbells back together above your chest along the same wide arc path.

{{% /steps %}}

{{< callout type="info" >}}
• Master proper form with lighter weights before increasing the load.

• Do not lower your elbows far below shoulder level, as this places excessive strain on your shoulder joints.

• Bring the dumbbells close together at the top to get a full squeeze in your chest muscles.

• Keep the weights moving directly over your upper chest—avoid letting them drift over your face or down toward your belly to protect your shoulders.
{{< /callout >}}
